# Repo-wide invariants

This rule is symlinked from `slab/.cursor/rules/00-always.mdc` into
every sibling project. It applies to all of Xiaoming Peng's
training-systems work (slab, MMOE, MonolithEP, Primus, Primus-dev,
RocMoE, …).

The **slab knowledge repo** at `~/workspace/slab/` is the single source
of truth for cross-project knowledge: hardware specs, library
distillations, paper notes, project work logs, rules, skills.

## Naming (for slab knowledge files and project docs)

- New files & directories: **kebab-case**, lowercase, ASCII.
- Each directory has **exactly one `README.md`**. No `README_<x>.md`
  siblings.
- Progress note: `YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_<topic>.md` (minute precision).
- Archive / paper note: `YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>.md` or `<slug>.md` for
  `slab/papers/`.

Application source code in sibling projects follows that project's own
style; these naming rules apply to docs / notes / configs added by the
agent, not to existing source files.

## Commits

- **Never** commit without an explicit user instruction.
- One logical concern per commit; never bundle unrelated edits.
- Imperative subject ≤ 72 chars.
- Project-specific commit / branch / PR conventions live in that
  project's `.cursor/rules/90-<project>-local.mdc`.

## Tone & formatting

- No emojis anywhere unless the user asks.
- Prefer tables over bullet lists when comparing ≥ 3 things across
  ≥ 2 attributes.
- Cite paths with backticks, never bare.

## Hardware context (default unless overridden)

AMD MI300X / MI325X / MI355X (CDNA3 / CDNA4); ROCm + PyTorch; SLURM;
Podman container `xiaoming-dev`. Comparison reference is NVIDIA
H100 / H200 / B200. Do not assume CUDA-only paths; both ROCm and CUDA
matter.

## Symlinked content — do not edit in-place

Files under `.cursor/rules/0[0-4]-*.mdc` and most directories under
`.cursor/skills/` in any sibling project are **symlinks back into slab**.
Editing them in-project affects every project. Always edit them in
`~/workspace/slab/` instead.

## When unsure

Grep `~/workspace/slab/knowledge/` then `~/workspace/slab/papers/`
then `~/workspace/slab/notes/` before asking. Never invent paper
titles, hardware specs, command flags, or paths.
